      "source": [
        "# Perform Full Fine-Tuning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "24f2d995",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "24f2d995"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Workflow\n",
        "\n",
        "# Model Fine-Tuning Roadmap\n",
        "\n",
        "- **t5-small** (original HuggingFace model)\n",
        "  - Fine-tuned on **SQL-Create-Context** / **Text-to-SQL** datasets\n",
        "- **finetuned_model_2_epoch**\n",
        "  - Further fine-tuned on **Spider** dataset\n",
        "- **finetuned_model_spider**\n",
        "  - Further fine-tuned on **harder datasets** or **custom user queries**\n",
        "- Final polished version can be fine tuned with as many datasets as possible!\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "This step-by-step fine-tuning strategy. Where each new training phase builds upon the previous one it mirrors **industry-standard practices** for developing production-ready models.  \n",
        "Top AI labs and companies (like OpenAI, Anthropic, Google DeepMind) **layer fine-tunes** progressively to adapt base models to increasingly complex and specialized tasks without forgetting earlier knowledge.  \n",
        "By mounting fine-tunes on top of each other, you achieve **higher specialization, better generalization, and faster convergence** compared to training from scratch each time.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Time Taken      = 28min 51s on A100\n",
        "\n",
        "Training Loss   = 0.019300\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "94988713",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "94988713"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "try:\n",
        "    finetuned_model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(\"finetuned_model_2_epoch\")\n",
        "    finetuned_model = finetuned_model.to('cuda')\n",
        "    to_train = False\n",
        "\n",
        "except:\n",
        "    to_train = True\n",
        "    finetuned_model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(model_name, torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n",
        "    finetuned_model = finetuned_model.to('cuda')\n",
        "    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)"
      ]
    },
